  "missing_reason": "MVTec AD and VisA are excluded: the perturbation needs BOTH levels for the same six configurations on the same units, and the repository's registered native-frame artifact (05_baselines/baseline_native_frame.csv) exists only for MPDD and BTAD, seed 0/1, K = 1/4.  No native-frame reading is fabricated.",
  "pairing": "the two levels of a perturbation share the same replicate draw of query images, so the interval describes the CHANGE, i.e. the two levels are paired on the image",
  "sampling_stream": "default_rng([20260913, dataset_id, category_id, replicate])",
  "bootstrap_grid": "the interval is computed on a subsample of the same grid: stride 8 where the frame is at least 64 px per side, otherwise the full grid.  The stride-8 affordability convention of the shared-region table is kept wherever it resolves the positives; on the 32x32 / 32x42 canvas patch grids it would collapse to 4x4 and can drop every positive pixel (observed on MPDD bracket_white), so those frames use stride 1.  Each row records its own `bootstrap_stride`."
